course: dictionary
lesson: 12056
title: Clams: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Clams is a good example. Read the words around it to find out which meaning the writer means. «We dug for clams on the beach.» Digging on a beach shows that clams are animals here.
explain: Clams are shellfish: animals with two hard shells joined by a hinge. They live in sand or mud. «The chef made clam chowder for lunch.» Chowder is a soup, so here clams are food.
explain: Clams can also be a verb. To clam up means to suddenly stop talking, often because you feel shy or scared. «When the teacher asked his name, Ben clammed up.» Ben stopped talking, so clam up means go silent. Ask yourself: does this word fit as a creature, a food, or an action?
fact: Clams is the plural of clam: one clam, two clams.
fact: A clam is a shellfish with two hard shells joined by a hinge.
fact: «To clam up» means to suddenly stop talking, often from shyness or fear.
fact: «Happy as a clam» means very happy. It is an American phrase.
fact: Giant clams on coral reefs can be huge.
exercise: Mia said, «Clams live in the sand.» What is a clam? | A soft, wet cloud | A kind of sandcastle | A tiny fish that swims very fast | *A shellfish with two hard shells joined by a hinge
exercise: «We dug for clams on the beach.» What are clams in this sentence? | Money | *Shellfish that live in sand | Birds that sing | Sweets
exercise: «When Ben was asked a question, he clammed up.» What does clammed up mean? | Ran away fast | Fell asleep | Shouted very loudly | *Suddenly stopped talking
test: «Grandma was happy as a clam at the lake.» What does happy as a clam mean? | Very tired | Very cold | Very hungry | *Very happy
test: Which is the plural of clam? | clamy | *clams | clammer | clamm
exam: Which sentence uses clams as food? | «The clams ran across the road.» | *«The chef served clam chowder for lunch.» | «I heard clams tapping on the door.» | «The clams sat quietly in the sand.»
